            <ArticleTitle>Risk stratification in patients with chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-118 ,vii</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the role of exercise testing in the assessment of patients with suspected coronary disease. To accomplish this, four major topics are considered: the general concept of risk stratification; the estimation of outcomes using data from the initial evaluation of the patient; diagnostic assessment with the exercise test; and prognostic assessment with the exercise test. This review focuses on the standard treadmill exercise test.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
